# Cursor subagent model policy

- Every Cursor subagent must run Grok 4.7 with `effort=xhigh`; no other model or effort is allowed.
- In subagent frontmatter (`.cursor/agents/*.md`), write `model: grok-4.7[effort=xhigh]`: a model ID plus bracketed `id=value` parameters.
- In `cursor-agent --model` or `/model`, use the flattened CLI ID `cursor-grok-4.7-xhigh`; do not put it in subagent frontmatter.
- Do not use `inherit`, `composer-*`, `auto`, a lower-effort model, or silent fallback.
- If the selector is unavailable, stop and report the dispatch as blocked.

This rule constrains Cursor subagent model selection only. It does not define any workflow or role process.
